#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adapt to changes in installing and depending on Qiskit v1.0"
msgstr ""
"Cómo adaptarse a los cambios en la instalación y las dependencias de Qiskit "
"v1.0"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install the new Qiskit v1.0 package"
msgstr "Instala el nuevo paquete Qiskit v1.0"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore jupyterlab, testenv */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore jupyterlab, testenv */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the new Qiskit v1.0 package {#install-the-new-qiskit-v10-package}"
msgstr ""
"Instala el nuevo paquete Qiskit v1.0 {#install-the-new-qiskit-v10-package}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit v1.0 uses a different packaging structure than previous Qiskit "
"versions and will likely cause problems in environments that use packages "
"that are not ready for Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit v1.0 utiliza una estructura de empaquetado diferente a la de "
"versiones anteriores de Qiskit, y es probable que cause problemas en "
"entornos que usen paquetes que aún no son compatibles con Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Do not try to upgrade an existing Python virtual environment to Qiskit v1.0 in-place.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"No intentes actualizar un entorno virtual de Python existente a Qiskit v1.0 en el mismo lugar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will not make similar breaking packaging changes in the future. This is a one-time event, at the release of Qiskit v1.0, specifically so that our packaging story will be as easy as possible in the future.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"No realizaremos cambios de empaquetado tan disruptivos en el futuro. Este es un evento único, en el lanzamiento de Qiskit v1.0, específicamente para que nuestra gestión de paquetes sea lo más sencilla posible de aquí en adelante.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide is divided into the following sections.  You only need to review "
"the sections that are relevant to you.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta guía está dividida en las siguientes secciones. Solo necesitas revisar "
"las que sean relevantes para ti.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Users should read the [For users](#for-users) section.\n"
msgstr "Los usuarios deben leer la sección [Para usuarios](#for-users).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you develop or maintain a package that depends on Qiskit, read the [For "
"developers](#for-developers) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si desarrollas o mantienes un paquete que depende de Qiskit, lee la sección "
"[Para desarrolladores](#for-developers).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you encounter problems installing or importing Qiskit v1.0, review the "
"[Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting) section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si encuentras problemas al instalar o importar Qiskit v1.0, revisa la "
"sección [Solución de problemas](#troubleshooting).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are interested in understanding the old package structure and why it "
"changed, review the [overview of the breaking package "
"changes](/guides/metapackage-migration).\n"
msgstr ""
"Si te interesa entender la estructura de paquetes antigua y por qué cambió, "
"consulta el [resumen de los cambios disruptivos de "
"empaquetado](/guides/metapackage-migration).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"for-users\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"for-users\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For users {#for-users}"
msgstr "Para usuarios {#for-users}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You must start a new virtual environment to install Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"It is very tricky and error-prone to upgrade an existing installation in-place to Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Debes crear un nuevo entorno virtual para instalar Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Actualizar una instalación existente a Qiskit v1.0 en el mismo lugar es muy complicado y propenso a errores.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The examples in this section use the `venv` module that is part of the Python standard library.\n"
"If you use a different tool, such as `virtualenv` or `conda`, consult its documentation for help.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Los ejemplos de esta sección usan el módulo `venv`, que forma parte de la biblioteca estándar de Python.\n"
"Si usas una herramienta diferente, como `virtualenv` o `conda`, consulta su documentación para obtener ayuda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For Linux and macOS commands, a bash-like syntax is used.\n"
"PowerShell is used for Windows commands.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Para los comandos de Linux y macOS se usa una sintaxis similar a bash.\n"
"Para los comandos de Windows se usa PowerShell.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"creating-a-venv\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"creating-a-venv\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create the new environment {#create-the-new-environment}"
msgstr "Crea el nuevo entorno {#create-the-new-environment}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a new virtual environment in each project directory you're working "
"in, using your preferred version of Python 3.8 or later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Crea un nuevo entorno virtual en cada directorio de proyecto en el que estés"
" trabajando, usando tu versión preferida de Python 3.8 o posterior.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<span id=\"activate\"></span>\n"
"2. Activate the environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"<span id=\"activate\"></span>\n"
"2. Activa el entorno.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```bash\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            .venv\\Scripts\\activate.ps1\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```powershell\n"
"            .venv\\Scripts\\activate.ps1\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install packages as desired.\n"
"You should do this by using only one `pip install` command with all the dependencies on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Instala los paquetes que necesites.\n"
"Lo ideal es hacerlo con un único comando `pip install` que incluya todas las dependencias.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   You can optionally include additional packages by including them as "
"arguments.  For example:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Opcionalmente puedes incluir paquetes adicionales como argumentos. Por "
"ejemplo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Qiskit v1.0 includes breaking changes, so several packages are marked as "
"not-yet-compatible with it.  Therefore, you might see errors from `pip` "
"until new versions of those packages are released. Old versions of packages "
"might also depend on the legacy `qiskit-terra` package.  Such packages might"
" not return errors when running this command, but might raise an error when "
"running `import qiskit`.  You should not install any packages that depend "
"directly on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Qiskit v1.0 incluye cambios disruptivos, por lo que varios paquetes están"
" marcados como aún no compatibles con él. Por eso, es posible que veas "
"errores de `pip` hasta que se publiquen nuevas versiones de esos paquetes. "
"Las versiones antiguas de algunos paquetes también pueden depender del "
"paquete heredado `qiskit-terra`. Esos paquetes podrían no devolver errores "
"al ejecutar este comando, pero sí lanzar un error al hacer `import qiskit`. "
"No deberías instalar ningún paquete que dependa directamente de `qiskit-"
"terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"   One way to require `pip` to forbid `qiskit-terra` from individual `install` commands is to use [a constraints file](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) that requires that `qiskit-terra` is set to an impossible version.\n"
"   For example, a constraints file that includes the line `qiskit-terra>=1.0` will mean that if a dependency attempts to install `qiskit-terra`, no published versions will match the requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"   Una forma de obligar a `pip` a prohibir `qiskit-terra` en comandos `install` individuales es usar [un archivo de restricciones](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) que establezca `qiskit-terra` en una versión imposible.\n"
"   Por ejemplo, un archivo de restricciones que incluya la línea `qiskit-terra>=1.0` hará que, si una dependencia intenta instalar `qiskit-terra`, ninguna versión publicada cumpla los requisitos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We have provided such a file in a GitHub Gist at "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), which "
"you can use like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Hemos proporcionado dicho archivo en un GitHub Gist en "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), que "
"puedes usar así:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   If a package requires `qiskit-terra`, you will see [a resolution failure](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   Si un paquete requiere `qiskit-terra`, verás [un fallo de resolución](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"   Do not install packages that are incompatible with Qiskit v1.0 on this virtual environment.  If you need to use such packages, install them in a separate virtual environment with Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"   No instales paquetes incompatibles con Qiskit v1.0 en este entorno virtual. Si necesitas usar esos paquetes, instálalos en un entorno virtual separado con Qiskit 0.45 o 0.46.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   If you have an existing environment, you can use "
"[`pipdeptree`](https://github.com/tox-"
"dev/pipdeptree/blob/main/README.md#pipdeptree) to query the requirements of "
"your installed packages to see if they require `qiskit<1`.  For any that "
"require `qiskit<1`, check for updates that make it compatible with Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Si tienes un entorno existente, puedes usar "
"[`pipdeptree`](https://github.com/tox-"
"dev/pipdeptree/blob/main/README.md#pipdeptree) para consultar los requisitos"
" de tus paquetes instalados y ver si alguno requiere `qiskit<1`. Para los "
"que lo requieran, busca actualizaciones que los hagan compatibles con Qiskit"
" v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   If you encounter issues, consult the [troubleshooting](#troubleshooting) "
"section, or ask on [Qiskit Slack](https://qisk.it/join-slack). If you think "
"there is a bug, you can [create an issue against "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Si encuentras problemas, consulta la sección de [solución de "
"problemas](#troubleshooting), o pregunta en [Qiskit "
"Slack](https://qisk.it/join-slack). Si crees que hay un error, puedes [crear"
" un issue en Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are not planning to use the environment immediately, use the "
"`deactivate` command to leave it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si no vas a usar el entorno de inmediato, usa el comando `deactivate` para "
"salir de él.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"activating-a-venv\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"activating-a-venv\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use the new environment {#use-the-new-environment}"
msgstr "Usa el nuevo entorno {#use-the-new-environment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each time you start a new command line session, you must navigate to your "
"project directory and \"activate\" the environment by running the `activate`"
" command:\n"
msgstr ""
"Cada vez que inicies una nueva sesión de línea de comandos, debes navegar al"
" directorio de tu proyecto y \"activar\" el entorno ejecutando el comando "
"`activate`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"for-developers\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"for-developers\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For developers {#for-developers}"
msgstr "Para desarrolladores {#for-developers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you maintain a package that depends on Qiskit, use this information to "
"learn how to correctly express your compatibility and test against Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si mantienes un paquete que depende de Qiskit, usa esta información para "
"aprender a expresar correctamente tu compatibilidad y a probar contra Qiskit"
" v1.0.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Recommendations for requirements {#recommendations-for-requirements}"
msgstr ""
"Recomendaciones para los requisitos {#recommendations-for-requirements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We recommend that your package requires `qiskit>=0.45,<1` (or other appropriate lower bound) if you are not certain whether the package is compatible with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"This is [the same recommendation being made for NumPy 2.0 compatibility](https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/24300).\n"
msgstr ""
"Recomendamos que tu paquete requiera `qiskit>=0.45,<1` (u otro límite inferior apropiado) si no estás seguro de si el paquete es compatible con Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Esta es [la misma recomendación que se hace para la compatibilidad con NumPy 2.0](https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/24300).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Qiskit v1.0 release candidate, version 1.0.0rc1, will be released on 1 February 2024.\n"
"You should test your package against this, and as soon as possible, release a new (compatible) version of your package with its upper requirement unpinned.\n"
msgstr ""
"Se publicará un candidato a lanzamiento de Qiskit v1.0, la versión 1.0.0rc1, el 1 de febrero de 2024.\n"
"Deberías probar tu paquete contra esta versión y, lo antes posible, publicar una nueva versión (compatible) de tu paquete con el requisito superior sin fijar.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recommendations for testing against Qiskit v1.0 {#recommendations-for-"
"testing-against-qiskit-v10}"
msgstr ""
"Recomendaciones para probar contra Qiskit v1.0 {#recommendations-for-"
"testing-against-qiskit-v10}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These recommendations apply to testing proactively against the Qiskit `main`"
" branch, and to testing against the v1.0.0rc1 (and later, if applicable) "
"release candidate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Estas recomendaciones aplican tanto a las pruebas proactivas contra la rama "
"`main` de Qiskit como a las pruebas contra el candidato a lanzamiento "
"v1.0.0rc1 (y versiones posteriores, si aplica).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We do not recommend initially branch-protecting on CI success against the Qiskit `main` branch because Qiskit changes could prevent you from merging PRs.\n"
"After the release of Qiskit release candidates, and after all of your package's dependencies support Qiskit v1.0, we *do* recommend branch-protecting on success against the latest release candidate, to ensure that the package remains compatible with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"No recomendamos proteger ramas en CI con éxito contra la rama `main` de Qiskit inicialmente, porque los cambios en Qiskit podrían impedirte fusionar PRs.\n"
"Después del lanzamiento de los candidatos a lanzamiento de Qiskit, y cuando todas las dependencias de tu paquete soporten Qiskit v1.0, *sí* recomendamos proteger ramas con éxito contra el último candidato a lanzamiento, para garantizar que el paquete siga siendo compatible con Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If neither your package, nor any of its transitive dependencies, has a requirement pin on `qiskit<1`, you should create a testing virtual environment as you normally would, in a single `pip install` command, and directly specify `qiskit==1.0.0rc1` or `qiskit==git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main` as appropriate.\n"
"This is the most reliable way to ensure that you have a completely valid environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si ni tu paquete ni ninguna de sus dependencias transitivas tiene un requisito fijado en `qiskit<1`, deberías crear un entorno virtual de pruebas como lo harías normalmente, en un único comando `pip install`, y especificar directamente `qiskit==1.0.0rc1` o `qiskit==git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main` según corresponda.\n"
"Esta es la forma más confiable de asegurarte de tener un entorno completamente válido.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the only component of your package's dependency graph that has a requirement pin on `qiskit<1` is your own package, you might want to have your CI suite first temporarily patch your requirements file to allow Qiskit v1.0, and then install the environment in a single step as before.\n"
"Alternatively, use the following rules for general-purpose environment upgrades, but switch to single-environment resolution as soon as feasible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si el único componente del grafo de dependencias de tu paquete que tiene un requisito fijado en `qiskit<1` es tu propio paquete, puede que quieras que tu suite de CI parchee temporalmente tu archivo de requisitos para permitir Qiskit v1.0 e instale el entorno en un solo paso como antes.\n"
"Alternativamente, usa las siguientes reglas para actualizaciones de entorno de propósito general, pero cambia a la resolución de entorno único tan pronto como sea posible.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If at least one of your transitive dependencies does not yet have a release version that allows Qiskit v1.0 support, you must make manual changes.\n"
"There are several strategies to try, in approximate order of preference (most preferable to least):\n"
msgstr ""
"Si al menos una de tus dependencias transitivas aún no tiene una versión publicada que permita el soporte de Qiskit v1.0, deberás hacer cambios manuales.\n"
"Hay varias estrategias que puedes intentar, en orden aproximado de preferencia (de más a menos preferible):\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the problematic dependency from its own `main` branch, if its "
"development version has relaxed the pin, so you can build the test "
"environment in a single step.\n"
msgstr ""
"Instala la dependencia problemática desde su propia rama `main`, si su "
"versión de desarrollo ya ha relajado el pin, para que puedas construir el "
"entorno de pruebas en un solo paso.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exclude the use of that dependency from the test environment, if possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Excluye el uso de esa dependencia del entorno de pruebas, si es posible.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a test environment in the same way you would normally, and then "
"manually override it to use Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Crea un entorno de pruebas de la misma forma que lo harías normalmente, y "
"luego anúlalo manualmente para usar Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Manually upgrade an existing environment {#manually-upgrade-an-existing-"
"environment}"
msgstr ""
"Actualizar manualmente un entorno existente {#manually-upgrade-an-existing-"
"environment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"This process deliberately creates an invalid environment.  Therefore, any test using it is less valid. Tests might appear to pass, but this does not guarantee that the package is compatible with Qiskit v1.0.  This could happen because the environment is not self-consistent and could contain files that do not exist in a valid environment, or the behavior of an overridden package might change with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Este proceso crea deliberadamente un entorno inválido. Por lo tanto, cualquier prueba que lo use es menos válida. Las pruebas podrían parecer que pasan, pero esto no garantiza que el paquete sea compatible con Qiskit v1.0. Esto puede ocurrir porque el entorno no es autoconsistente y podría contener archivos que no existen en un entorno válido, o porque el comportamiento de un paquete anulado podría cambiar con Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If one of your dependencies pins `qiskit<1` even on their development branch, it might not work in any way with Qiskit v1.0, and if your tests cannot run because of this, you might have to wait for them (or work with them) to become compatible.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Si una de tus dependencias fija `qiskit<1` incluso en su rama de desarrollo, es posible que no funcione de ninguna manera con Qiskit v1.0, y si tus pruebas no pueden ejecutarse por esto, puede que tengas que esperar a que sean compatibles (o trabajar con ellos para lograrlo).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To upgrade an environment in situ, follow these steps:\n"
msgstr "Para actualizar un entorno en el lugar, sigue estos pasos:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create an environment as usual, ensuring that there are no packages that "
"extend the `qiskit` or `qiskit.providers` namespace installed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Crea un entorno de la forma habitual, asegurándote de que no haya paquetes "
"instalados que extiendan el espacio de nombres de `qiskit` o "
"`qiskit.providers`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Uninstall both `qiskit` and `qiskit-terra` to make sure that neither is "
"present:\n"
msgstr ""
"Desinstala tanto `qiskit` como `qiskit-terra` para asegurarte de que ninguno"
" esté presente:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  At this point, the environment's `site-packages` should not contain a `qiskit` directory. You don't need to verify this on every CI run, but if you are debugging a script locally, follow these steps to verify:\n"
"  1. Run the following command from within the `python` of the virtual environment:\n"
msgstr ""
"  En este punto, el directorio `site-packages` del entorno no debería contener un directorio `qiskit`. No es necesario verificar esto en cada ejecución de CI, pero si estás depurando un script localmente, sigue estos pasos para comprobarlo:\n"
"  1. Ejecuta el siguiente comando desde dentro del `python` del entorno virtual:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import site\n"
"    print(site.getsitepackages())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  2. Verify that those directories do not contain a `qiskit` directory. If they do, you likely have namespace-extending packages installed, and you should find these and remove the dependency.\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```python\n"
"    import site\n"
"    print(site.getsitepackages())\n"
"    ```\n"
"  2. Verifica que esos directorios no contengan un directorio `qiskit`. Si lo contienen, probablemente tienes instalados paquetes que extienden el espacio de nombres y deberías encontrarlos y eliminar la dependencia.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the target version of Qiskit v1.0 with one of these commands:\n"
msgstr "Instala la versión objetivo de Qiskit v1.0 con uno de estos comandos:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "After the  desired release candidate has been published:\n"
msgstr "Una vez publicado el candidato a lanzamiento deseado:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'qiskit==1.0.0rc1'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  * For a `main`-branch dependency (or substitute whatever `git` revision identifier you prefer after the `@`).\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'qiskit==1.0.0rc1'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  * Para una dependencia de la rama `main` (o sustituye el identificador de revisión `git` que prefieras después del `@`):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main'\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```bash\n"
"    pip install 'git+https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit.git@main'\n"
"    ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You now have an environment that Qiskit allows you to test in. If `import "
"qiskit` results in an `ImportError`, or if you are struggling to find your "
"dependencies, see the advice in the section about the  [invalid-environment "
"protections](#qiskit-1.0-import-error) in Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora tienes un entorno en el que Qiskit te permite hacer pruebas. Si "
"`import qiskit` produce un `ImportError`, o si tienes dificultades para "
"encontrar tus dependencias, consulta el apartado sobre las [protecciones de "
"entorno inválido](#qiskit-1.0-import-error) en Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sample manual GitHub Actions workflows {#sample-manual-github-actions-"
"workflows}"
msgstr ""
"Ejemplos de flujos de trabajo manuales para GitHub Actions {#sample-manual-"
"github-actions-workflows}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following workflows set up a scheduled job to run overnight.  This job "
"sets up a testing environment for Qiskit v1.0 and runs `pytest` (or whatever"
" test steps you need).\n"
msgstr ""
"Los siguientes flujos de trabajo configuran un trabajo programado para "
"ejecutarse cada noche. Este trabajo prepara un entorno de pruebas para "
"Qiskit v1.0 y ejecuta `pytest` (o los pasos de prueba que necesites).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For a package that has no transitive dependencies `qiskit<1`:\n"
msgstr "Para un paquete que no tiene dependencias transitivas con `qiskit<1`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a package that has unavoidable transitive dependencies that pin "
"`qiskit<1`, build an invalid environment:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para un paquete que tiene dependencias transitivas inevitables que fijan "
"`qiskit<1`, construye un entorno inválido:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sample `tox` configuration {#sample-tox-configuration}"
msgstr "Ejemplo de configuración de `tox` {#sample-tox-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following are examples of `tox.ini` sections to build a testing "
"environment for Qiskit v1.0 and run `pytest` (or whatever test steps you "
"need).\n"
msgstr ""
"Los siguientes son ejemplos de secciones de `tox.ini` para construir un "
"entorno de pruebas para Qiskit v1.0 y ejecutar `pytest` (o los pasos de "
"prueba que necesites).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If nothing prevents Qiskit v1.0 from being installed in a valid "
"environment:\n"
msgstr "Si nada impide que Qiskit v1.0 se instale en un entorno válido:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your package or a transitive dependency has an unavoidable pin on `qiskit<1`, we recommend doing this testing using the manual environment construction as in the above section, because `tox` introduces several complexities by being more strict about environment isolation and installation order.\n"
"This is correct behavior by `tox` (we shouldn't construct an invalid environment), but because we already know we're building an invalid environment, these checks get in the way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si tu paquete o una dependencia transitiva tiene un pin inevitable en `qiskit<1`, recomendamos hacer estas pruebas usando la construcción manual del entorno como en la sección anterior, porque `tox` introduce varias complejidades al ser más estricto sobre el aislamiento del entorno y el orden de instalación.\n"
"Este es el comportamiento correcto de `tox` (no deberíamos construir un entorno inválido), pero como ya sabemos que estamos construyendo un entorno inválido, estas comprobaciones se interponen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"troubleshooting\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"troubleshooting\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting {#troubleshooting}"
msgstr "Resolución de problemas {#troubleshooting}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The packaging changes around Qiskit v1.0 are tricky, and Python's standard tool `pip` is not rich enough in some ways for us to communicate the changes in the distribution structures to it, which unfortunately might cause issues for users.\n"
"We have tried to make Qiskit fail quickly and loudly if it detects an invalid environment, without false positives.\n"
"We understand that users might find it annoying to get the error message, but in our experience, it's much better to be aware of the problem right away than for things to appear to be working on the surface, only to fail in subtle ways in the future.\n"
msgstr ""
"Los cambios de empaquetado en torno a Qiskit v1.0 son complicados, y la herramienta estándar de Python `pip` no es suficientemente expresiva en algunos aspectos para que podamos comunicarle los cambios en las estructuras de distribución, lo que lamentablemente puede causar problemas a los usuarios.\n"
"Hemos intentado que Qiskit falle de forma rápida y explícita si detecta un entorno no válido, sin generar falsos positivos.\n"
"Entendemos que puede resultar molesto recibir el mensaje de error, pero en nuestra experiencia es mucho mejor ser consciente del problema de inmediato que aparentar que todo funciona correctamente para luego fallar de forma sutil en el futuro.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section contains packaging errors that you might see, and describes how"
" to resolve them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta sección contiene errores de empaquetado que podrías encontrar y "
"describe cómo resolverlos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Most of these problems are not unique to Qiskit, so the advice is likely "
"relevant, even if the problematic parts are not related to Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"La mayoría de estos problemas no son exclusivos de Qiskit, por lo que el "
"consejo probablemente sea relevante aunque las partes problemáticas no estén"
" relacionadas con Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`import qiskit` says \"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'qiskit'\" "
"{#import-qiskit-says-modulenotfounderror-no-module-named-qiskit}"
msgstr ""
"`import qiskit` indica \"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'qiskit'\" "
"{#import-qiskit-says-modulenotfounderror-no-module-named-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Python cannot find your Qiskit installation.\n"
msgstr "Python no puede encontrar tu instalación de Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you definitely installed Qiskit, then you probably do not have the correct virtual environment activated.\n"
"See the [section on activating a virtual environment](#activating-a-venv) for instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si definitivamente instalaste Qiskit, probablemente no tienes el entorno virtual correcto activado.\n"
"Consulta la [sección sobre cómo activar un entorno virtual](#activating-a-venv) para obtener instrucciones.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are using Jupyter and see this, ensure that Jupyter is installed into the same virtual environment as Qiskit.\n"
"Exit Jupyter, activate the Qiskit virtual environment on the command line, run `pip install jupyterlab` (or whichever notebook interface you use), then reopen Jupyter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si estás usando Jupyter y ves esto, asegúrate de que Jupyter esté instalado en el mismo entorno virtual que Qiskit.\n"
"Sal de Jupyter, activa el entorno virtual de Qiskit en la línea de comandos, ejecuta `pip install jupyterlab` (o la interfaz de notebook que uses) y vuelve a abrir Jupyter.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`import qiskit` succeeds, but trying to do anything returns "
"\"AttributeError: module 'qiskit' has no attribute '...'\" {#import-qiskit-"
"succeeds-but-trying-to-do-anything-returns-attributeerror-module-qiskit-has-"
"no-attribute}"
msgstr ""
"`import qiskit` tiene éxito, pero intentar hacer cualquier cosa devuelve "
"\"AttributeError: module 'qiskit' has no attribute '...'\" {#import-qiskit-"
"succeeds-but-trying-to-do-anything-returns-attributeerror-module-qiskit-has-"
"no-attribute}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This likely means that your environment had an old version of Qiskit in it alongside a package that extended its namespace (such as old versions of Qiskit Aer, or the long-obsolete Qiskit IBM Q&reg; Provider), and then Qiskit was uninstalled.\n"
"The easiest thing to do is to start a new virtual environment, and only install recent, non-obsolete packages into it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Probablemente esto significa que tu entorno tenía una versión antigua de Qiskit junto con un paquete que extendía su espacio de nombres (como versiones antiguas de Qiskit Aer, o el ya obsoleto Qiskit IBM Q&reg; Provider), y luego Qiskit fue desinstalado.\n"
"Lo más sencillo es iniciar un nuevo entorno virtual e instalar únicamente paquetes recientes y no obsoletos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you have just started a new virtual environment, or you're sure that legacy packages are not the problem, make sure that your current working directory (the directory your shell session was in when you launched Python / Jupyter) does not contain a folder called `qiskit`.\n"
"Python's default rules search the current working directory very early in the search path when trying to `import` a module, so a directory with a duplicate name can cause import problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si acabas de crear un nuevo entorno virtual, o estás seguro de que los paquetes heredados no son el problema, asegúrate de que tu directorio de trabajo actual (el directorio en el que estaba tu sesión de shell cuando lanzaste Python / Jupyter) no contenga una carpeta llamada `qiskit`.\n"
"Las reglas predeterminadas de Python buscan en el directorio de trabajo actual muy al principio de la ruta de búsqueda al intentar hacer `import` de un módulo, por lo que un directorio con un nombre duplicado puede causar problemas de importación.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pip-resolution-impossible\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"pip-resolution-impossible\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`pip` refuses to install some packages together {#pip-refuses-to-install-"
"some-packages-together}"
msgstr ""
"`pip` se niega a instalar algunos paquetes juntos {#pip-refuses-to-install-"
"some-packages-together}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After running a `pip install` command with many items on it, you might see "
"an error such as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Después de ejecutar un comando `pip install` con varios elementos, podrías "
"ver un error como el siguiente:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This describes a true resolution conflict; there is no valid way to install "
"all of these distributions at the same time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto describe un conflicto de resolución real; no hay ninguna forma válida "
"de instalar todas estas distribuciones al mismo tiempo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the context of Qiskit v1.0, this is likely because one of the distributions you are trying to install contains a requirement like `qiskit<1.0`.\n"
"This means that the developers of that distribution have marked it as not (yet) compatible with Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"En el contexto de Qiskit v1.0, probablemente se deba a que una de las distribuciones que intentas instalar contiene un requisito como `qiskit<1.0`.\n"
"Esto significa que los desarrolladores de esa distribución la han marcado como (aún) no compatible con Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can (politely) ask those developers when they will release a new version of their package that is compatible with Qiskit v1.0, but first check that they have no open issue or pull request already asking for this wherever they accept comments.\n"
"Be mindful that this takes time; please give the developers a month or so to prepare new versions of their distributions!\n"
"Until then, you cannot install that distribution alongside Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"To continue using that distribution, create a new virtual environment and use Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46 (or whichever version it supports) alongside that other package.\n"
msgstr ""
"Puedes pedir (amablemente) a esos desarrolladores cuándo publicarán una nueva versión de su paquete compatible con Qiskit v1.0, pero primero comprueba si ya hay algún issue o pull request abierto que solicite esto en el lugar donde aceptan comentarios.\n"
"Ten en cuenta que esto lleva tiempo; ¡por favor, dale a los desarrolladores un mes más o menos para preparar nuevas versiones de sus distribuciones!\n"
"Hasta entonces, no puedes instalar esa distribución junto con Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Para seguir usando esa distribución, crea un nuevo entorno virtual y usa Qiskit 0.45 o 0.46 (o la versión que soporte) junto con ese otro paquete.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"If you get this error, **do not** try to build the environment by calling `pip install` several times.\n"
"Those commands will probably not fail, but you will have created an invalid environment.\n"
"You would likely then see some of the other error messages described in this section.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Si recibes este error, **no** intentes construir el entorno llamando a `pip install` varias veces.\n"
"Esos comandos probablemente no fallarán, pero habrás creado un entorno no válido.\n"
"Es probable que luego veas algunos de los otros mensajes de error descritos en esta sección.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can also read [the documentation from the Python packaging authority "
"about conflict resolution](https://pip.pypa.io/en/latest/topics/dependency-"
"resolution/#dealing-with-dependency-conflicts).\n"
msgstr ""
"También puedes leer [la documentación de la Python Packaging Authority sobre"
" resolución de conflictos](https://pip.pypa.io/en/latest/topics/dependency-"
"resolution/#dealing-with-dependency-conflicts).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`pip` succeeds but prints errors after running `pip install` commands {#pip-"
"succeeds-but-prints-errors-after-running-pip-install-commands}"
msgstr ""
"`pip` tiene éxito pero imprime errores tras ejecutar comandos `pip install` "
"{#pip-succeeds-but-prints-errors-after-running-pip-install-commands}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You might see an error in the output of `pip`, such as the following:\n"
msgstr "Podrías ver un error en la salida de `pip`, como el siguiente:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The top line usually appears verbatim (as of `pip` 23.3), but second line changes depending on the exact problem, and there may be several lines like it.\n"
"`pip` is likely to then indicate that it did whatever you wanted successfully, despite the error message.\n"
msgstr ""
"La primera línea suele aparecer exactamente igual (a partir de `pip` 23.3), pero la segunda línea varía según el problema exacto, y puede haber varias líneas similares.\n"
"Es probable que `pip` indique luego que hizo lo que solicitaste correctamente, a pesar del mensaje de error.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means that the environment is in conflict and you cannot be sure that it will work correctly.\n"
"To solve the problem, examine the list of messages from `pip` and determine if you need all of the packages that have conflicting requirements.\n"
"Sometimes there will be true conflicts between dependencies; you might need multiple virtual environments to separate out dependencies that have incompatible requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto significa que el entorno tiene conflictos y no puedes estar seguro de que funcionará correctamente.\n"
"Para resolver el problema, examina la lista de mensajes de `pip` y determina si necesitas todos los paquetes que tienen requisitos en conflicto.\n"
"A veces habrá conflictos reales entre dependencias; puede que necesites varios entornos virtuales para separar dependencias con requisitos incompatibles.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The safest choice is to begin a new virtual environment (or more than one, "
"if there are true conflicts), then delete the one in conflict.\n"
msgstr ""
"La opción más segura es crear un nuevo entorno virtual (o más de uno si hay "
"conflictos reales) y eliminar el que está en conflicto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When setting up virtual environments, run only one `pip install` command that includes all the dependencies you need.\n"
"This is the most reliable way for `pip` to find a properly resolved environment with no conflicts.\n"
"If you keep having problems with conflicts after setting up environments, avoid running any further `pip install` or `pip uninstall` commands; `pip` does not guarantee to keep the environment coherent on subsequent commands.\n"
msgstr ""
"Al configurar entornos virtuales, ejecuta solo un comando `pip install` que incluya todas las dependencias que necesitas.\n"
"Esta es la forma más fiable para que `pip` encuentre un entorno correctamente resuelto sin conflictos.\n"
"Si sigues teniendo problemas con conflictos al configurar entornos, evita ejecutar más comandos `pip install` o `pip uninstall`; `pip` no garantiza mantener el entorno coherente en comandos posteriores.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you are concerned about working with multiple virtual environments, rest assured that Python development and use often involve several virtual environments. It's common and good practice to create new ones to work on separate projects.\n"
"When you're done with a virtual environment, you can simply delete its directory; there is no reason to keep multiple environments permanently.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Si te preocupa trabajar con varios entornos virtuales, ten la seguridad de que el desarrollo y el uso de Python a menudo implican varios entornos virtuales. Es habitual y una buena práctica crear nuevos para trabajar en proyectos separados.\n"
"Cuando hayas terminado con un entorno virtual, simplemente puedes eliminar su directorio; no hay ninguna razón para mantener varios entornos de forma permanente.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit-1.0-import-error\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"qiskit-1.0-import-error\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`import qiskit` raises `ImportError` {#import-qiskit-raises-importerror}"
msgstr ""
"`import qiskit` lanza `ImportError` {#import-qiskit-raises-importerror}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When running `import qiskit`, you might see an error such as:\n"
msgstr "Al ejecutar `import qiskit`, podrías ver un error como:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
" ImportError: Qiskit is installed in an invalid environment that has both Qiskit 1.0+ and an earlier version.\n"
" You should create a new virtual environment, and ensure that you do not mix dependencies between Qiskit pre-1.0 and post-1.0.\n"
" Any packages that depend on 'qiskit-terra' are not compatible with Qiskit 1.0 and will need to be updated.\n"
" Qiskit unfortunately cannot enforce this requirement during environment resolution.\n"
msgstr ""
" ImportError: Qiskit is installed in an invalid environment that has both Qiskit 1.0+ and an earlier version.\n"
" You should create a new virtual environment, and ensure that you do not mix dependencies between Qiskit pre-1.0 and post-1.0.\n"
" Any packages that depend on 'qiskit-terra' are not compatible with Qiskit 1.0 and will need to be updated.\n"
" Qiskit unfortunately cannot enforce this requirement during environment resolution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"You might have run a completely valid `pip install` command, following all the recommendations in this guide, and still see this error message.\n"
"This is not your fault, but the error message is still correct, and Qiskit cannot safely load.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"Es posible que hayas ejecutado un comando `pip install` completamente válido, siguiendo todas las recomendaciones de esta guía, y aun así ver este mensaje de error.\n"
"Esto no es culpa tuya, pero el mensaje de error sigue siendo correcto y Qiskit no puede cargarse de forma segura.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The error means that Qiskit is installed in an invalid environment that includes both Qiskit v1.0 and an earlier version.\n"
"This is characterized by the `qiskit-terra` distribution being installed alongside Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"You can check what distributions are installed by running `pip list`, but you cannot fix this by simply uninstalling `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"El error significa que Qiskit está instalado en un entorno no válido que incluye tanto Qiskit v1.0 como una versión anterior.\n"
"Esto se caracteriza porque la distribución `qiskit-terra` está instalada junto con Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Puedes comprobar qué distribuciones están instaladas ejecutando `pip list`, pero no puedes solucionar esto simplemente desinstalando `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, `qiskit>=1.0` and `qiskit-terra` are conflicting distributions, and cannot both be installed together.\n"
"Even more unfortunately, *we cannot communicate this conflict to `pip`* because of limitations in its metadata system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lamentablemente, `qiskit>=1.0` y `qiskit-terra` son distribuciones en conflicto y no pueden estar instaladas juntas.\n"
"Más lamentablemente aún, *no podemos comunicar este conflicto a `pip`* debido a las limitaciones de su sistema de metadatos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This error most frequently arises in one of two situations:\n"
msgstr ""
"Este error surge con mayor frecuencia en una de estas dos situaciones:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '*  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You ran something like `pip install 'qiskit>=1' something-else`, and "
"`something-else` has a requirement on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ejecutaste algo como `pip install 'qiskit>=1' something-else` y `something-"
"else` tiene un requisito sobre `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '*  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You tried to run `pip install -U qiskit` in an existing environment.\n"
msgstr "Intentaste ejecutar `pip install -U qiskit` en un entorno existente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In both of these cases, there is no guarantee that `pip` will return a "
"helpful message to you.\n"
msgstr ""
"En ambos casos, no hay garantía de que `pip` te devuelva un mensaje útil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"tip\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to require `pip` to forbid `qiskit-terra` from individual `install` commands is to use [a constraints file](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) that requires that `qiskit-terra` is set to an impossible version.\n"
"For example, a constraints file that includes the line `qiskit-terra>=1.0` will mean that if a dependency attempts to install `qiskit-terra`, no published versions will match the requirements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una forma de exigir a `pip` que prohíba `qiskit-terra` en comandos `install` individuales es usar [un archivo de restricciones](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/#constraints-files) que establezca `qiskit-terra` en una versión imposible.\n"
"Por ejemplo, un archivo de restricciones que incluya la línea `qiskit-terra>=1.0` significará que si una dependencia intenta instalar `qiskit-terra`, ninguna versión publicada coincidirá con los requisitos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We have provided such a file in a GitHub Gist at "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), which "
"you can use like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Hemos proporcionado dicho archivo en un GitHub Gist en "
"[https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints](https://qisk.it/1-0-constraints), que "
"puedes usar así:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If a package requires `qiskit-terra`, you will see [a resolution "
"failure](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
msgstr ""
"Si un paquete requiere `qiskit-terra`, verás [un fallo de resolución](#pip-"
"resolution-impossible).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-1.0\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-1.0\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a working environment for Qiskit v1.0 {#create-a-working-environment-"
"for-qiskit-v10}"
msgstr ""
"Crear un entorno funcional para Qiskit v1.0 {#create-a-working-environment-"
"for-qiskit-v10}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No matter how this happened, it is much easier to make a new virtual "
"environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"No importa cómo haya ocurrido esto, es mucho más fácil crear un nuevo "
"entorno virtual.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we need to find out which packages are introducing a dependency on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"Using the broken environment, install `pipdeptree` from PyPI. This is a tool for generating dependency graphs:\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero, necesitamos averiguar qué paquetes están introduciendo una dependencia en `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"Usando el entorno roto, instala `pipdeptree` desde PyPI. Esta es una herramienta para generar grafos de dependencias:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ask it which packages are introducing dependencies on `qiskit-terra` and "
"`qiskit` (these are two separate commands):\n"
msgstr ""
"Pregúntale qué paquetes están introduciendo dependencias en `qiskit-terra` y"
" `qiskit` (estos son dos comandos separados):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The outputs might look something like:\n"
msgstr "Las salidas pueden verse algo así:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above example, we have two distributions that have declared "
"themselves compatible with Qiskit v1.0 (`qiskit-aer` and `qiskit-ibm-"
"provider`), and one that still has a dependency on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"En el ejemplo anterior, tenemos dos distribuciones que se han declarado "
"compatibles con Qiskit v1.0 (`qiskit-aer` y `qiskit-ibm-provider`), y una "
"que aún tiene una dependencia en `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"This example is a flat dependency structure.\n"
"You might see a much deeper tree than this.\n"
"The packages that are directly dependent on `qiskit-terra` (lowest indentation) are most likely to be the problematic ones, but one farther down the tree could be problematic if it depends on a specific old version of some other package that has already been updated.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"Este ejemplo tiene una estructura de dependencia plana.\n"
"Es posible que veas un árbol mucho más profundo que este.\n"
"Los paquetes que dependen directamente de `qiskit-terra` (con menor indentación) son los que tienen más probabilidades de ser problemáticos, aunque uno más profundo en el árbol también podría serlo si depende de una versión específica y antigua de algún otro paquete que ya ha sido actualizado.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Seeing a dependency on `qiskit-terra` can mean one of a few things:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ver una dependencia en `qiskit-terra` puede significar una de varias "
"cosas:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dependent is an old package, and will not be updated to support Qiskit "
"v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"El dependiente es un paquete antiguo que no se actualizará para admitir "
"Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In this case, there is no chance of using the package with Qiskit v1.0, and you will need to continue using a previous version of Qiskit.\n"
"  Typically this is characterized by the dependent being at its latest version (assuming the environment is new, and you didn't pin it lower) and having a direct requirement on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"  En este caso, no hay posibilidad de usar el paquete con Qiskit v1.0 y tendrás que seguir usando una versión anterior de Qiskit.\n"
"  Normalmente esto se caracteriza porque el dependiente está en su última versión (suponiendo que el entorno sea nuevo y no lo hayas fijado a una versión inferior) y tiene un requisito directo sobre `qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dependent is a package that is actively maintained, but does not yet "
"support Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"El dependiente es un paquete que se mantiene activamente, pero aún no admite"
" Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In this case, you will need to wait for the developers to release a compatible version - please be patient!\n"
"  Typically this is characterized by the installed distribution *not* being at its latest version, even though your installation command did not specify a version.\n"
"  You can check the latest release version of the distribution by finding its page on https://pypi.org/.\n"
msgstr ""
"  En este caso, tendrás que esperar a que los desarrolladores publiquen una versión compatible; ¡por favor, sé paciente!\n"
"  Normalmente esto se caracteriza porque la distribución instalada *no* está en su última versión, aunque tu comando de instalación no especificara una versión.\n"
"  Puedes comprobar la última versión publicada de la distribución buscando su página en https://pypi.org/.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  `pip` likely searched old versions of the package until it found one "
"(possibly from months or years ago) that depended only on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"  `pip` probablemente buscó versiones antiguas del paquete hasta encontrar "
"una (posiblemente de hace meses o años) que dependía únicamente de `qiskit-"
"terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This is what has happened in the example above.  At the time this document"
" was created, `qiskit-dynamics==0.4.4` was the latest release version.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Esto es lo que ocurrió en el ejemplo anterior. En el momento en que se "
"creó este documento, `qiskit-dynamics==0.4.4` era la última versión "
"publicada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you constructed this environment out of several `pip install` commands (such as if the environment is old and has been updated), first try to install all of your packages by using a single `pip install` command when you build a new environment.\n"
"If the problem persists, at least one of the packages you want likely does not support Qiskit v1.0 yet, and `pip` is finding an old version that it believes will work because it doesn't know about the `qiskit>=1`/`qiskit-terra` conflict.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si construiste este entorno con varios comandos `pip install` (por ejemplo, si el entorno es antiguo y ha sido actualizado), intenta primero instalar todos tus paquetes usando un único comando `pip install` al crear un nuevo entorno.\n"
"Si el problema persiste, al menos uno de los paquetes que deseas probablemente no admite Qiskit v1.0 todavía, y `pip` está encontrando una versión antigua que cree que funcionará porque desconoce el conflicto `qiskit>=1`/`qiskit-terra`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead, use the `pipdeptree` commands to identify which dependencies do not yet support Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Exclude any packages that do not yet support Qiskit v1.0 when constructing a Qiskit v1.0 environment, or continue to use a prior version of Qiskit.\n"
"See [Create the new environment](#creating-a-venv) for instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"En su lugar, usa los comandos de `pipdeptree` para identificar qué dependencias aún no admiten Qiskit v1.0.\n"
"Excluye cualquier paquete que no admita todavía Qiskit v1.0 al construir un entorno para Qiskit v1.0, o sigue usando una versión anterior de Qiskit.\n"
"Consulta [Crear el nuevo entorno](#creating-a-venv) para obtener instrucciones.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The example in this section was generated before Qiskit v1.0 was released.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"El ejemplo de esta sección se generó antes del lanzamiento de Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The \"old\" distribution in question (`qiskit-dynamics`) was behaving correctly; it was not known to support Qiskit v1.0 yet, so it marked that in its requirements.\n"
"It's not possible to backdate requirements changes to previously released versions, and `pip` will search arbitrarily far back to locate something that works when building an environment.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"La distribución \"antigua\" en cuestión (`qiskit-dynamics`) se estaba comportando correctamente; no se sabía que admitía Qiskit v1.0 todavía, por lo que lo indicó en sus requisitos.\n"
"No es posible actualizar retroactivamente los cambios de requisitos en versiones publicadas anteriormente, y `pip` buscará arbitrariamente hacia atrás para encontrar algo que funcione al construir un entorno.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-0.45\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"debug-venv-for-0.45\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a working environment for Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46 {#create-a-working-"
"environment-for-qiskit-045-or-046}"
msgstr ""
"Crear un entorno funcional para Qiskit 0.45 o 0.46 {#create-a-working-"
"environment-for-qiskit-045-or-046}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you have a broken environment after trying to install Qiskit 0.45 or 0.46, the most likely situation is that `pip` installed Qiskit v1.0 because it tried to pick the latest versions of packages, even though it was not required.\n"
"The easiest way to fix this is to create a new virtual environment, then run a single `pip install` command that has all the packages you need, plus an explicit `'qiskit<1'` entry.\n"
"If `pip` successfully resolves this dependency graph, you should have a working virtual environment.\n"
"If at least one distribution requires Qiskit v1.0 or greater, `pip` should give you an error message explaining this, which looks like the one in [the section on failed resolutions](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"
msgstr ""
"Si tienes un entorno roto después de intentar instalar Qiskit 0.45 o 0.46, la situación más probable es que `pip` haya instalado Qiskit v1.0 porque intentó elegir las últimas versiones de los paquetes, aunque no fuera necesario.\n"
"La forma más sencilla de solucionarlo es crear un nuevo entorno virtual y ejecutar un único comando `pip install` que incluya todos los paquetes que necesitas, más una entrada explícita `'qiskit<1'`.\n"
"Si `pip` resuelve correctamente este grafo de dependencias, deberías tener un entorno virtual funcional.\n"
"Si al menos una distribución requiere Qiskit v1.0 o superior, `pip` debería darte un mensaje de error explicándolo, similar al de [la sección sobre resoluciones fallidas](#pip-resolution-impossible).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can also use the `pipdeptree` commands listed in [Create a working "
"environment for Qiskit 1.0](#debug-venv-for-1.0) from within the broken "
"environment to determine which distributions have an explicit requirement on"
" `qiskit>=1`.\n"
msgstr ""
"También puedes usar los comandos de `pipdeptree` listados en [Crear un "
"entorno funcional para Qiskit v1.0](#debug-venv-for-1.0) desde dentro del "
"entorno roto para determinar qué distribuciones tienen un requisito "
"explícito en `qiskit>=1`.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I'm a developer, my environments are definitely right, and I'm still getting"
" the error {#im-a-developer-my-environments-are-definitely-right-and-im-"
"still-getting-the-error}"
msgstr ""
"Soy desarrollador, mis entornos están definitivamente bien y sigo obteniendo"
" el error {#im-a-developer-my-environments-are-definitely-right-and-im-"
"still-getting-the-error}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First: you must be *absolutely* certain that your environments are correct.\n"
"The test that Qiskit uses to determine a broken environment is quite robust; specifically, it queries `importlib.metadata` for distribution information on installed packages and checks the version numbers returned.\n"
"The Qiskit v1.0 side of the test also checks for sentinel files that were present in old Qiskit versions and not Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero: debes estar *absolutamente* seguro de que tus entornos son correctos.\n"
"La prueba que usa Qiskit para determinar si hay un entorno roto es bastante robusta; concretamente, consulta `importlib.metadata` para obtener información de distribución sobre los paquetes instalados y comprueba los números de versión devueltos.\n"
"El lado de Qiskit v1.0 de la prueba también busca archivos centinela que estaban presentes en versiones antiguas de Qiskit y no en Qiskit v1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are a Qiskit developer, it's possible that you have old `qiskit.egg-info` or `qiskit-terra.egg-info` (or `*.dist-info`) directories present on your meta path (see `sys.meta_path`), left over from old editable installations.\n"
"In particular, check your working directory for any `*.egg-info` and `*.dist-info` directories.\n"
"If they're in the root of one of your checked out repositories, you can delete them. The worst that can happen is you might need to `pip install -e .` again, and even that is unlikely, because these are typically just part of the `setuptools` build process that doesn't get cleaned up.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si eres un desarrollador de Qiskit, es posible que tengas directorios `qiskit.egg-info` o `qiskit-terra.egg-info` (o `*.dist-info`) antiguos presentes en tu meta path (consulta `sys.meta_path`), que quedaron de instalaciones editables antiguas.\n"
"En particular, revisa tu directorio de trabajo en busca de directorios `*.egg-info` y `*.dist-info`.\n"
"Si están en la raíz de uno de tus repositorios clonados, puedes eliminarlos. Lo peor que puede pasar es que necesites ejecutar `pip install -e .` de nuevo, y eso es poco probable, ya que normalmente son solo parte del proceso de construcción de `setuptools` que no se limpia automáticamente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the above information does not help you and you are 100% sure that your "
"environment is sound (or you are deliberately trying to test a broken "
"environment):\n"
msgstr ""
"Si la información anterior no te ayuda y estás 100% seguro de que tu entorno"
" es correcto (o estás deliberadamente intentando probar un entorno roto):\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Create an issue in "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose) explaining how "
"this happened and why you are sure the environment is correct so we can fix "
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Crea un issue en "
"Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/new/choose) explicando cómo "
"ocurrió esto y por qué estás seguro de que el entorno es correcto para que "
"podamos solucionarlo.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can suppress the exception by setting the environment variable "
"`QISKIT_SUPPRESS_1_0_IMPORT_ERROR=1`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Puedes suprimir la excepción estableciendo la variable de entorno "
"`QISKIT_SUPPRESS_1_0_IMPORT_ERROR=1`.\n"
